#T Megadungeon of the Mad Archmage Gary-Stu, Level 3: Mazes

#R *Wandering Monsters*\
#R In Area 4, Cynthia will arrive on a 1 on a roll of d20 (check each round); otherwise she will be in the center.
#R
#R Check every turn: 1 in 12 chance of one of the dwarf children showing up.\
#R
#R No other wandering monsters on this level; it's not very friendly to them.

#K *Room Key*
#K *Grand Stairway*: up to surface, down to level 8.
#K + *Gelatinous Cube Maze*: Cubes start at a, b, c. Move in straight lines, choose randomly at forks, don't reverse unless they hit a dead end. Gelatinous Cube: (AC 3; HP 22, 24, 29; Slam + 2 melee, 1d6 + 1d6 acid + paralyze, engulf DC 13/DEX (engulfed creatures take 1d6 acid damage per round), paralysis 1d12 rounds, DC 13/STR). Each cube has 2d8 gp, 2d4 pp, bits of glass, 1d2 base 10 gp gems.
#K + *Hubert's Lair*: Hubert (AC 15; HP 26; Claw + 2 / Claw + 2 / Bite + 3 (1d6/1d6/1d12). If both claws hit, he can hug that target for 2d8 each additional round.) is an owlbear mage. He knows only one spell, _Shocking Grasp_. He has 33 gp, a folio-sized spellbook written in crayon, several mundane books (worth 1-4 gp each), a bottle full of green vapor, when broken or opened casts _Stinking Cloud_, and a potion of _Invisibility_.
#K + *Minotaur Labyrinth*: Cynthia the Minotaur (AC 15; HP 37; Greataxe + 6 1d12+4 or Gore + 5 1d8+4) lives in the center of the labyrinth. She'd welcome the Flesh Vats for a change of pace, and so will fight to the death on almost any pretext. She has a ruby necklace worth 200 gp, a small chest containing 25 pp and a potion of _Cure Moderate Wounds_, and a _Nose Ring Of Protection +1_(could be worn as a bracelet by small characters; only works as nose ring).
#K + *Watering Hole*: Cindy and Grono come here to drink or to chat with the Longbeards. Water is clean.
#K + *Grono's Room*: Grono (AC 17; HP 16; Morningstar +5, 1d8+3) is a down-on-his-luck bugbear (pumpkin-headed variety). He resents having to live by the sewer stairs, and would join an adventuring party if offered a decent bribe.
#K + *Janice Longbeard's Shop*: Janice runs the shop with her husband Tommy. They have 3 children, Rita, Ronnie, and Gwen. The children are noncombatants (AC 12, HP 4, 4), while Janice and Tommy will fight if they must (AC 16 [chain mail]; HP 11, 11; Waraxe + 5 (1d8+2)).  If approached nicely and treated with respect, Janice knows almost everything there is to know down as far as the Crypts. If the party are jerks, prices will go up, and everyone else in the dungeon will know about it. If the Longbeards are killed, Gary-Stu will be very pissy if he meets the party.
#K + *Longbeards' Kitchen/Larder*: Surprisingly good selection of foodstuffs and spices here. Worth about 75gp in all, if the party is that jerkish.
#K + *Longbeards' Living Room*: The children will be found here, playing jacks for copper pieces. It's a dwarven ale-hall in miniature, basically.  The children sleep on cots in here.
#K + *Janice and Tommy's Bedroom*: Janice and Tommy keep their fortune in a strongbox here (DC 22 to force open, key is in Janice's pocket). 1208 gp, 227 pp, potions of _Super-Heroism_ and _Cure Moderate Wounds_. There's also a pearl locket with a cameo of a dwarven matron (Janice's mother) worth 55 gp, and two sets of silver his-and-hers beard-combs, brushes, picks, ties, and braid adornments. These were an anniversary present to each other.
#K + *Toilets*.
#K + *Ennis and Jack's Ranch House*: Ennis and Jack are ogres (AC 16; HP 30, 28; Greatclub + 7 (1d8+4)). They will fight to the death to protect one another, but are not hostile to visitors unless attacked first, or unless someone starts being a homophobe. Each has 22 sp, 2 lb. of chewing tobacco, and an ogre-sized 10-gallon hat.
#K + *Ennis and Jack's Bedroom*: Unguents and fragrant oils and perfumes worth 125 gp. Assless chaps (Ogre-sized) worth 25 gp to the right buyer.
#K + *Brokeback Cavern*: Rothe (AC 13, HP 9, Gore + 2 (1d4)) herd (26, plus + 5 calves (HP 3 each; noncombatant). They eat moss and lichen in the cavern, and Ennis and Jack occasionally sell them to raise money.
#K + *Teleporter Maze*: 15.1 - 15.5 are cross-shaped halls of mirrors. A teleports to A, B to B, etc.
#K + *Pit to Sewers*: 30' drop. 1d6 damage; land in muck.
